# Copy to .env.local and fill in real values. This documents the config the
# app needs as the mock-data/localStorage service layer
# (src/modules/<domain>/*Service.js, src/services/*.js) is swapped for the
# real backend (see docs/ENGINEERING_BLUEPRINT.md, backend/).
#
# Hosting: Cloudflare Pages (frontend, this repo) + Cloudflare Workers (backend
# API, translation, auth) — see wrangler.toml. Cloudflare account credentials
# (API token, account ID) are deploy-time secrets in CI/the Workers project's
# own wrangler config, NOT client-side REACT_APP_* vars — a token prefixed
# REACT_APP_ ships inside the browser bundle, which would leak it publicly.

# Base URL for the Cloudflare Workers backend API (backend/, see its README).
# Shared by every *Service.js that's been switched over so far — each gated
# behind its own feature flag in src/config/featureFlags.js, so this one URL
# being set doesn't turn everything on at once:
#   - src/modules/auth/authService.js  → `realAuthApi`
#   - src/modules/books/booksService.js → `realBooksApi` (syncs the catalogue
#     once at app boot via src/index.js's bootstrap(), not per-request)
#   - src/services/userService.js → `realProgressApi` (reading progress/stats)
#   - src/modules/reading/bookmarksService.js → `realBookmarksApi` (book- and
#     page-level bookmarks)
#     Both hydrate their localStorage cache once per session — app boot if
#     already signed in, or right after login/register (see AuthContext.js) —
#     and mirror writes to the API in the background, not per-request.
#   - src/modules/auth/authService.js's getAllUsers()/setUserRole()
#     (the /admin/users page) → `realUserManagementApi` — no localStorage
#     cache; calls the API directly since it has exactly one call site.
# Until both a service's flag AND this URL are set, it keeps using its
# localStorage mock unchanged.
REACT_APP_API_BASE_URL=
